WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.000
Ask most people about the things that are important to them, about what really matters in their life and what makes them happy. And you'll hear a common refrain, my spouse or partner, my children, my family, my closest friends. Close relationships are essential to our happiness and well-being, and decades of research have shown that they're also important predictors of physical health. Why is that? What kind of support do we receive from our partners and other close relationships,
问大多数人什么对他们最重要，生命中最在乎什么，以及什么能让他们快乐，你都会听到一个共同的答案：我的配偶或伴侣、我的孩子、我的家人、我最亲密的朋友。亲密关系对我们的幸福感和健康至关重要，几十年的研究表明，它们也是身体健康的重要预测指标。这是为什么呢？我们从伴侣和其他亲密关系中获得了什么样的支持，

2
00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:58.000
and why does that support matter so much? What are the biological mechanisms that tie together social relationships and health? What are the ingredients of a good and supportive relationship and how do we develop these deep ties to each other? Also, how has the COVID-19 pandemic affected our close relationships? Are people coming out of the past year and a half feeling a stronger connection to their loved ones or have those ties frayed? And what, if any, lasting effects might we see?
这种支持为什么如此重要？将社会关系和健康联系在一起的生物学机制是什么？一段良好且相互支持的关系的要素是什么，我们又是如何培养彼此之间这种深厚联系的？此外，COVID-19疫情对我们的亲密关系产生了怎样的影响？在经历过去的一年半之后，人们与挚爱的联系是变得更强了，还是这些纽带已经磨损？如果说有什么持久的影响的话，我们可能会看到什么？

