Much of your research has focused specifically on marriages and other long-term intimate relationships. Are these benefits true for other close relationships too? I mean, you just talked about nuns, so they must be right. I mean, because nuns aren't married, and married to Jesus, they're married to God. But what about other close friendships and family relationships? Are the benefits that people derive equivalent to the benefits that they might get from a long-term intimate partner? Absolutely. I mean, when I think about the size of the effects that we see for intimate relationships,
你的许多研究都特别集中在婚姻和其他长期亲密关系上。这些益处对其他亲密关系也同样适用吗？我的意思是，你刚才谈到了修女，所以它们一定适用，对吧？我的意思是，因为修女没有结婚，与耶稣结婚，她们是嫁给了上帝。但其他亲密友谊和家庭关系呢？人们从这些关系中获得的益处，是否等同于他们从长期亲密伴侣那里获得的益处？绝对是的。我的意思是，当我想到我们看到的亲密关系的效应大小时，

9
